        "predictedCite": "presented one of the very first articles successfully analyzing the gene/metabolite associations in a gene-to-metabolite network via the integration of time-series transcriptome and metabolome datasets. The authors used a correlation-based approach to identify the gene-metabolite associations and then used the identified associations to predict the metabolite levels at the next time point. The authors showed that the predicted metabolite levels were highly correlated with the actual metabolite levels.\n\nIn this study, we propose a novel approach to predict the metabolite levels at the next time point using the gene expression data and the gene-metabolite associations. The proposed approach is based on the assumption that the metabolite levels at the next time point can be predicted by the gene expression levels at the current time point and the gene-metabolite associations. The proposed approach is evaluated using the time-series transcriptome and metabolome datasets of Arabidopsis thaliana. The results show that the proposed approach can predict the metabolite levels at the next time point with high accuracy.\n\n# Methods\n\n# Datasets\n\nThe"
