        "actualCite": "Massive Abelian gauge symmetries and fluxes in F-theory, Grimm",
        "predictedCite": "it was in fact suggested, on the basis of the supergravity analysis, that in F-theory models with a smooth Type IIB limit the selection rules associated with massive U (1)s continue to be present. This is in contrast to the situation in heterotic models, where the selection rules associated with massive U (1)s are lifted in the smooth limit. This is because in the smooth limit the gauge group is enhanced to a non-Abelian group, and the massive U (1)s are broken by the Higgs mechanism. In F-theory models, however, the gauge group is always Abelian, and the massive U (1)s are not broken by the Higgs mechanism. Thus, the selection rules associated with massive U (1)s are expected to be present in F-theory models with a smooth Type IIB limit.\n\n# 4.2.2. The case of a non-Abelian gauge group\n\nIn the case of a non-Abelian gauge group, the massless spectrum is given by (4.1). The"
